<title>MONACO: TENNIS-LEADING ATP RANKINGS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-LEADING ATP RANKINGS.</headline>
<dateline>MONACO 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gustavo Kuerten of Brazil has</p>
<p>jumped from 66th to 15th in the latest ATP rankings after</p>
<p>winning the French Open at the weekend:</p>
<p>  1. Pete Sampras (U.S.)		   4,699 points</p>
<p>  2. Michael Chang (U.S.)		  3,727</p>
<p>  3. Goran Ivanisevic (Croatia)	  2,803</p>
<p>  4. Thomas Muster (Austria)	     2,769</p>
<p>  5. Richard Krajicek (Netherlands)    2,449</p>
<p>  6. Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)	 2,279</p>
<p>  7. Alex Corretja (Spain)		 2,208</p>
<p>  8. Sergi Bruguera (Spain)		2,176</p>
<p>  9. Thomas Enqvist (Sweden)	     2,148</p>
<p> 10. Carlos Moya (Spain)		   2,119</p>
<p> 11. Marcelo Rios (Chile)		  2,092</p>
<p> 12. Albert Costa (Spain)		  1,820</p>
<p> 13. Boris Becker (Germany)		1,819</p>
<p> 14. Alberto Berasategui (Spain)	 1,803</p>
<p> 15. Gustavo Kuerten (Brazil)	    1,763</p>
<p> 16. Felix Mantilla (Spain)		1,743</p>
<p> 17. Patrick Rafter (Australia)	  1,707</p>
<p> 18. Andrei Medvedev (Russia)	    1,613</p>
<p> 19. Mark Philippoussis (Australia)    1,579</p>
<p> 20. Todd Martin (U.S.)		    1,578</p>
</text>
